-- title:
--   Gauss ring at an ∞-branch cusp descends to level qM' (q=2)
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q=2$, let $M'\ge 1$ with $q\nmid M'$, let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero containing a primitive $q$-th root of unity $\zeta$ such that some ring homomorphism $L\to\mathbb C$ carries $\zeta$ to $e^{2\pi i/q}$, and let $L$ be algebraic over $\mathbb Q$. Let $K\subseteq L(\!(t)\!)$ be the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of the function field of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$ with $H$ the kernel of $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal, $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, uniformiser $\varpi$, and acting on $K$ compatibly; let $j\in K$ be nonzero with Laurent expansion the $q$-expansion of $j$. Let $W_0\subseteq K$ be the valuation subring of those $f$ for which $f\cdot y=x$ for some power series $x,y$ over $A$ with $y$ having nonzero reduction. Write $\mathfrak X$ for the two-chart integral model of $K$ over $A$ attached to $j$ (the pushout of the spectra of the integral closures of $A[j]$ and $A[j^{-1}]$ in $K$). Let $z\in\mathfrak X$ be a point at which the global image of $\varpi$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, and let $y\in\operatorname{Spec}$ of the integral closure $A_\infty$ of $A[j^{-1}]$ in $K$ be a maximal ideal mapping to $z$, with $j^{-1}\in\mathfrak p_y$ and with every $b\in A_\infty$ that is a non-unit of $W_0$ lying in $\mathfrak p_y$. Let $K_0\subseteq K_0'\subseteq K$ be the $L$-subfields generated by the coefficientwise images of the $q$-expansion function fields of $\Gamma_0(M')$ and $\Gamma_0(qM')$, with $O_0\subseteq K_0$, $O_0'\subseteq K_0'$ the valuation subrings defined by the same power-series condition as $W_0$. Then, for the algebra structures given by these inclusions, every valuation subring $B$ of $K$ whose contraction to $K_0$ is $O_0$ and such that every $b\in A_\infty$ which is a non-unit of $B$ lies in $\mathfrak p_y$ has contraction to $K_0'$ equal to $O_0'$.
--
--   This is the cusp-side statement on the pole chart: a vertical valuation whose centre passes through a cusp on the $\infty$-branch of the Igusa-type integral model, and which induces the Gauss valuation at level $M'$, already induces the Gauss valuation at level $qM'$; in the classical language this identifies the component of the reduction of $X_0(qM')$ below such a point as the $\infty$-type one (Deligne–Rapoport, Katz–Mazur). It is the $q=2$ case, and it feeds the unramifiedness statement [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.isUnramifiedAt_of_height_one_of_algebraMap_mem_chartAlgInf_of_jInvChartInf_mem_xH_of_eq_two`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.isUnramifiedAt_of_height_one_of_algebraMap_mem_chartAlgInf_of_jInvChartInf_mem_xH_of_eq_two).
